00:02:46,000 --> 00:03:15,360
抜かしていればいい 傷を恐れ羽ばたかる人生なんて悪性と変わらない 人は一生夢と感動くらい生きてく 痛いくらい羽の腎臓 鳥肌が止まらない 命が熱く燃えている

41
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:38,280
限界の先 その先で戦う喜びは 勝ち負けすらもどこか遠く 時を止めたこの一瞬が スローモーションで煌めく

42
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:41,120
さあ暴れな

43
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:50,600
技を強いに過労しかて 彼は想しみない

44
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,320
Just one touch

45
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:53,500
ってるからです

46
00:03:53,500 --> 00:04:05,460
頑張って troupeを games色々 牧場でカラズノの好き

47
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:14,840
が中 AFPは愛して高さを 成功し上げて粘着大な

48
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:21,160
Damn it that should have been a good one

49
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,840
It's the same as always

50
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:30,660
What's your deal? We got the point, right? If you have something to say say it

51
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:37,480
Yeah, right if he told you what to do you'd start pushing back

52
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:43,900
I mean if you really think Kageyama knows how to accurately express his thoughts, then you've totally lost your damn mind

53
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:45,740
Yeah, no kidding

54
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:51,800
But still it's not new for him to be overly critical or to say things in the meanest way possible

55
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,440
So it's weird that he's not doing that

56
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:13,580
Dang he's a freaking robot a guy can barely keep his balance in that position, but he sends the ball to the perfect spot

57
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:19,400
Not too high or too low not too close or too far. How much has this guy practiced?

58
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:22,200
I'm kind of getting emotional

59
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:32,620
Damn it all sorry guys, no worries

60
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:36,400
Maybe they're a little too afraid of those blocks

61
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,240
Go go let's go let's go day tech

62
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,240
Yeah

63
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:46,780
Don't mind us. We're just here to cheer on our precious junior teammates

64
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:50,740
We don't want to get in the way or anything, so we'll just go watch from upstairs

65
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:54,240
Hey you three this isn't your school, you know

66
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:56,240
That's all right. We don't mind

67
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,240
I'm sorry about this

68
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:01,580
Hey, hey, you guys better not lose today

69
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:04,080
Show them what date tech tradition is all about

70
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:08,120
Go go let's go let's go date tech

71
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,920
Thanks, we'll do our best

72
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:14,300
Well, they must have a lot of free time on their hands

73
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:16,900
What was that, Futakuchi? We can hear you, you know

74
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:18,660
Come on, let me hear you guys out here

75
00:06:18,660 --> 00:06:21,700
When we get a point, I want you to scream your lungs out

76
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:25,740
Futakuchi, look at you now all grown up and leading the team

77
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:29,200
There's more than one way for us to apply some pressure to our opponent

78
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:33,080
We're gonna break their spirits and we'll do it just enough that the rest don't really notice

79
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:36,620
If you can't do it in a practice game, you won't be able to do it in a real one

80
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:41,520
Way to go Futakuchi, you turd

81
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:43,160
Shut your trap, Kamasaki

82
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:48,240
Well, if nothing else, I'm glad date tech is having fun today

83
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:55,240
Ah, sorry

84
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:59,980
Is it me or is Kurasuno not playing that great?

85
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,580
No doubt, we could actually win this damn thing

86
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:07,620
Quick

87
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:09,000
Damn

88
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:13,060
Nice kill

89
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:16,120
Hey, Tsukishima, you were supposed to jump again

90
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:18,340
You had enough time for another one

91
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:23,680
Uh, I'm pretty sure Tsuki really doesn't need him to point that out right now

92
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:27,480
Oh, why are we so irritable?

93
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:31,220
Is His Majesty an ill-humor today?

94
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:32,980
Huh?

95
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:36,740
Well, uh

96
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:39,720
Tsukishima's usually a little better at taking criticism

97
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:41,380
Guess Kageyama's the exception

98
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:44,020
Yeah, I don't think that's really the case

99
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,480
Those two just don't get along

100
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:47,480
Ooh, this is not good

101
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:49,520
So, should we call timeout?

102
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:50,720
Not quite yet

103
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,760
They'll sort it out

104
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:57,360
Taiji!

105
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:07,840
Out!

106
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,560
Asahi, you're freaking awful today, man

107
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,700
What's going on?

108
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:12,700
Ah, damn it

109
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:13,200
Sorry

110
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,760
Your set was just fine

111
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:16,400
Then score the damn point

112
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,860
Uh-uh

113
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:18,840
Ah

114
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:19,780
Hmm

115
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:26,920
Asahi, you need to stop

116
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:53,520
Oh, uh, hey, Kageyama, check this out.

117
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:54,520
There's something I want to...

118
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,480
Just shut up and listen!

119
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:59,380
The sets I'm giving you are excellent!

120
00:08:59,380 --> 00:09:01,660
You need to start scoring some points!

121
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:15,360
Look, everyone, we've seen the return of the king.

122
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:18,440
If your sorry asses ever expect to win anything,

123
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:21,060
you better learn to adapt to the way I set!

124
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:35,120
I apologize.

125
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:39,040
You know, I always wondered, what's wrong with Kageyama being the king?

126
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,360
Is it that he's too self-centered?

127
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:43,880
Or that he's bossy?

128
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:48,940
I mean, either way, it doesn't really matter!

129
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:51,520
If I don't agree with what he says, I just ignore him!

130
00:09:51,520 --> 00:10:00,240
He can be completely right, but well, if he's a dick, no way I'm gonna do it!

131
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,840
I agree with what he said.

132
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:03,660
Yeah, okay, Tanaka, whatever.

133
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:06,680
If someone gives you instructions, you're totally gonna follow him.

134
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:09,520
Just because you're so strict about maintaining team etiquette.

135
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:10,500
Yeah, true.

136
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:14,540
Well, I would appreciate it if you were a little more nice about stuff.

137
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:19,040
See? It doesn't really matter if you're the king or not.

138
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:23,020
Oh, come on, man!

139
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:25,480
Isn't being a king supposed to be, like, awesome?

140
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:32,560
There is no better set than the one that is easy for the spiker to hit.

141
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:37,440
And it's definitely true that you only find out what that is by communicating.

142
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:41,620
But, man, I really don't think that means you're not gonna fight sometimes.

143
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:46,900
Have you considered why you're having trouble responding to Small Fry's request?

144
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:49,000
Do you even want to put in the effort at all?

145
00:10:49,780 --> 00:10:52,020
Was that last set decent enough for you, punk?

146
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:55,960
Hmm, I think I could probably hit it a little bit faster.

147
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:57,460
So a little zippier, maybe?

148
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:58,360
I can do that.

149
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:01,060
You're just a goody-two-shoes.

150
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:06,760
Uh, I'm sorry, Kageyama.

151
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:11,520
I've been trying to time my hits in a way where they don't match Date Tech's block attempts.

152
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:14,900
But I still can't quite get it to work against these guys.

153
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:16,500
Your sets are great, though.

154
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,380
So keep doing what you're doing.

155
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:23,480
They're probably gonna keep blocking me for a while, so I'll apologize now.

156
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:24,700
My bad.

157
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:27,980
And I'm still trying that super-sharp cut shot!

158
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:31,400
I mean, what better time than practicing against Date Tech?

159
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:33,100
And you can just deal with it.

160
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:35,500
I can't promise I will.

161
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:38,960
Ha ha ha ha!

162
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:40,400
Fine with me!

163
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:41,660
Ha ha ha ha!

164
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,040
Ha ha ha ha ha!

165
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,880
We're starting the second set!

166
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:48,840
So they're...fighting?

167
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:53,620
Well, it's not like you fight just because someone told you that you need to have a fight.

168
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:55,960
I mean, it happens.

169
00:11:56,560 --> 00:12:01,280
If Kageyama's starting to tell the guys what's on his mind, how about if they try telling him?

170
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:06,020
Kageyama is so extremely talented.

171
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:10,880
It's possible that the other members of the team haven't quite figured out how to criticize his play yet.

172
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:12,760
Hey! You're not attacking from the middle end of today!

173
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,100
What's up, Kageyama? You scared or something?

174
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:16,020
What?!

175
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:17,540
We need to go down the middle more!

176
00:12:17,620 --> 00:12:19,860
Hinata's right compared to all their other games.

177
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:21,360
He is going there less.

178
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:24,860
I guess there is one guy who can call him out on stuff.

179
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:25,900
Ha ha ha ha ha!

180
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:28,520
Nice save!

181
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:32,100
Let's try one and a half ball widths.

182
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,100
Ah, son of a...

183
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:38,860
He didn't make it!

184
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:45,960
How are they ever going to survive this spring playing the way they are?

185
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:48,580
Although, I guess it's not like I actually care.

186
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:51,180
I guess even Kageyama makes mistakes too!

187
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:53,180
Hey!

188
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:54,080
Hmm?

189
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:58,120
I will not baby you.

190
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:00,520
Oh? Really?

191
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:03,060
Well, I wasn't exactly expecting you to.

192
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:12,700
Kageyama does actually try to get along with people sometimes, and it's not like he was saying anything that came totally out of left field.

193
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:17,260
So, do you think maybe he's still a little bothered by the feud he had when he was in middle school?

194
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:20,900
He doesn't really seem like the type of person who would get stuck in the past, though.

195
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:23,940
People are weighed down by different things.

196
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:25,700
Middle school, or...

197
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,540
His past?

198
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:30,580
Whatever happened must be a super heavy weight for him.

199
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:34,220
Yeah, still.

200
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:37,720
I don't know all the details and whatnot, but one thing's for sure.

201
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:44,520
Kageyama's gotten to a point where he understands that there's a distinct possibility he might be wrong about certain things.

202
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:50,640
And that's a fact his middle school teammates probably forced him to realize by hitting him over the head with it.

203
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:55,360
One touch!

204
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,580
Chance ball, everyone!

205
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:06,640
He jumped!

206
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:13,400
Before, Kageyama would adjust to accommodate all of the spikers' quirks.

207
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:18,280
But now he's setting it out of reach to get the spiker to hit it from higher up.

208
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:26,820
Oh, man!

209
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:28,800
Dang, that was up there!

210
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:30,040
Hmph.

211
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:42,380
You jumped that time.

212
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:44,480
Kageyama!

213
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:45,940
Way to look smug, buddy!

214
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:48,720
Suki, settle down and remember, keep your mind still!

215
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:50,840
Kageyama, stop trying to provoke Suki!

216
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:52,900
Will you shut up, Tadashi?

217
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:58,020
It's the greatest position there is because you get to be the ruler!

218
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:04,940
The setter is the team's control tower!

219
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:07,740
It's the position that gets the most contact with the ball!

220
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:11,340
It's the greatest position there is because you get to be the ruler!

221
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:14,040
Come on now, don't act all surprised.

222
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:16,000
You know I wouldn't forget you said that.

223
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:19,200
Act like a goody-goody all you want.

224
00:15:19,740 --> 00:15:21,460
Deep down, you'll always be the king.

225
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:23,860
Prepare yourself!

226
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:32,820
From this day on, you shall be known as the new king of the cards!

227
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:56,280
Well, looks like he's lettin' it go.

228
00:15:56,280 --> 00:16:07,400
I'm not good at figuring out people's feelings.

229
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:11,120
And apparently, I'm not exactly the best with words either.

230
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:12,220
Yeah, we know that.

231
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:16,220
This isn't breaking news, you know, but...

232
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:17,940
I will be the best setter.

233
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:19,460
Ever.

234
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:22,000
Yeah, yeah, we know.

235
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:26,000
It's not like you haven't made that perfectly clear.

236
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,200
Aw, listen to his majesty.

237
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:31,220
What a good little boy he's being.

238
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:32,020
Come on!

239
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:34,340
Tsukishima, do us all a favor and grow up!

240
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:35,720
That's coming from Hinata!

241
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:38,340
Someone's still a little mad about earlier, huh?

242
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:39,480
That's a nice face.

243
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:40,860
You smell something stinky?

244
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:42,700
Did you stop confusing things?

245
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:47,700
It's okay for me to be a goody-two-shoes here.

246
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:51,280
It's normal not to know what other people are feeling.

247
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:55,980
I mean, it's important for you to consider it.

248
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:59,040
But it's not absolutely necessary during a game.

249
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:01,680
Your jobs are the following things.

250
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:04,780
To know how the game is going and how your teammates are doing.

251
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:16,180
Oh, those two are way more in sync now.

252
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:17,880
Nice kill, Suki!

253
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:22,840
The longer Date Tech plays against us, the better their blocks get.

254
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:26,880
If I'd hit the ball from any lower, they would have totally shut me down.

255
00:17:27,620 --> 00:17:28,340
Oh, wow.

256
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:30,220
Tsukishima's always been a giant.

257
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:33,020
So I never would have thought of him as hitting the ball low or anything.

258
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:35,380
But he can hit from even higher than I thought.

259
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:36,580
That's what I said!

260
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:37,180
Yeah.

261
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:39,560
Looks like he hates doing it, though.

262
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:41,440
Kogane...

263
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:43,880
Uh, I mean, Date Tech's setter was setting for him.

264
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:46,220
And he would sometimes hit the ball from way up there.

265
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:46,720
Oh.

266
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:51,180
Tsukishima hits the ball really compact or whatever, and it sounds all like fa-bam, you know?

267
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,580
His swing is quick, too.

268
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:56,140
Well, a middle blocker's job is to attack as quickly as possible.

269
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:58,320
So I guess a lot of them are probably like that.

270
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:02,680
Well, a good setter would keep that speed in mind and set the ball lower, too.

271
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:06,900
But at the camp, Kogane was setting too high a lot of the time.

272
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:08,820
Sorry!

273
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:13,840
And when he messed up, I guess Tsukishima just did what he could.

274
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,800
He didn't really have much of a choice.

275
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:19,140
So he wound up trying to sync up with Kogane instead of settling.

276
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,040
Oh.

277
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:22,440
He's really paying attention.

278
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:25,540
Well, all my teammates are growing up.

279
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:26,620
No doubt.

280
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:29,720
You gotta give props to Kageyama for pulling it out of him.

281
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:33,080
But I'm not gonna stand here and let Tsukishima beat me in jumping height.

282
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,000
Yeah, well.

283
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:35,780
But I meant you, too.

284
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:41,460
Nice kill!

285
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:43,360
Keep him coming, I feel great!

286
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:43,660
No.

287
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:46,540
Sorry, Tanaka.

288
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:48,560
But your spikes are starting to get sloppy.

289
00:18:49,220 --> 00:18:52,060
If you're tired, we can bring someone else in to handle your spot.

290
00:18:52,060 --> 00:19:00,120
Yeah, I'm sure Kageyama only said that because he thought he was looking out for me.

291
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:00,960
I get it.

292
00:19:01,060 --> 00:19:01,540
I do.

293
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:02,460
But?

294
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:05,720
You're not subbing me out, dumbass!

295
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:08,560
And yeah, sure, that last hit was all power and no technique!

296
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:09,920
Whoa, he admitted it.

297
00:19:10,060 --> 00:19:11,140
I'm so proud.

298
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:14,320
It's not like Tanaka's totally wiped out, though.

299
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:18,840
But I do think we should use this to figure out what we would do in these particular situations.

300
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:25,940
In games, we'd rather sub people out to give ourselves an advantage instead of making up for problems.

301
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:27,040
Well, all right.

302
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,940
I'll send him fewer balls and keep my eye on him.

303
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:33,780
If you absolutely have to, could you at least be cool about it?

304
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:34,860
It's not like you can say,

305
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:37,080
You're cut off and I'll be all great, thank you!

306
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:38,640
Be cool?

307
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,300
Well, I can try.

308
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:44,060
Yo, for me, I actually do announce it.

309
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:49,600
If I look around and realized I wasn't getting the ball anymore, I think that would probably hurt my feelings.

310
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:50,300
So sensitive!

311
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:54,160
I will do my best, but I can't make any promises.

312
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:56,820
It's okay. You don't have to spoil them.

313
00:19:58,080 --> 00:19:59,580
They're constantly evolving.

314
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:04,380
That evolution might not always be a good thing for everyone all the time.

315
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:10,320
But with this group of second and third years, I think they'll be okay.

316
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:15,460
The third years are always talking about how glad they are we had such strong first years join.

317
00:20:16,140 --> 00:20:18,340
But I bet Kageyama's glad they're here too.

318
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:20,180
I'm sure.

319
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:25,540
Nice receive!

320
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:26,720
Kageyama!

321
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:27,960
Left side!

322
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:30,480
Might be a bit close to the net.

323
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:31,500
Let's try that again.

324
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:35,480
Sorry.

325
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:38,000
There's nothing to apologize for, Asahi!

326
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:39,880
Sorry.

327
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:42,100
Yeah, it was our job to pick up the slack there.

328
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:43,940
Right. Sorry.

329
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:46,740
He's getting yelled at and told not to apologize?

330
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:48,260
All at the same time.

331
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:49,780
Tanaka feeling okay?

332
00:20:50,180 --> 00:20:52,240
Yeah, I don't know what the hell he's doing.

333
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:55,160
Asahi has to be getting more and more confused.

334
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:58,920
Are we just ignoring the fact that Kageyama's set was off?

335
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:00,360
Sorry.

336
00:21:03,860 --> 00:21:07,520
I don't know what's going on here, but Kurashino seems off their game.

337
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:12,440
Let's crush him!

338
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:14,520
Asahi!

339
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:15,600
Over here!

340
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:17,440
Hinata, send it over!

341
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:19,200
Crap, it's short!

342
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:22,480
You're going to hear it!

343
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:27,820
Yeah!

344
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:28,060
Yeah!

345
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:30,700
I'm okay.

346
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:31,820
Give me a sec.

347
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:34,560
My bad, guys.

348
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:40,780
Throw the opponent off guard with a killer serve, then finish them off with a block.

349
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:43,300
It's the perfect serve-block combo!

350
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:50,000
As of right now, Daytech's only real standout server is their new captain.

351
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:57,380
But if they ever manage to train up any more good servers, they might just become untouchable.

352
00:21:57,380 --> 00:22:07,020
Well, next year, the team that ends up giving us the most trouble just might be Daytech.

353
00:22:07,020 --> 00:22:20,260
Well, next year, the team that ends up giving us the most trouble just might be Daytech.

354
00:22:20,260 --> 00:22:21,160
Daytech.

355
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:28,660
Daytower.

356
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:32,900
Daytower.

357
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:33,080
Daytower.

358
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:35,100
Daytower.

359
00:22:35,340 --> 00:22:35,740
Daytower.

360
00:22:35,740 --> 00:22:45,740
Pressure, that's why I need God. I don't need help.

361
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:56,740
Egoist, that's why I need God. I don't have a reason.

362
00:22:56,740 --> 00:23:01,740
We are...挑まずにはいられない。 影さえも振り切ってけ。

363
00:23:01,740 --> 00:23:06,740
現状の限界、乗り越えろチャンス。

364
00:23:06,740 --> 00:23:11,740
We are...戦力をかけた。 We are...怯えることない。

365
00:23:11,740 --> 00:23:17,740
We are...隠しへ変われ、高く、高く、高く、

366
00:23:17,740 --> 00:23:23,740
舞い上がれ、味わった敗北のキスは。

367
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:44,740
Hello!

